[{:db/id "q-330631/field-1/031aaf43793f128e0d888774b282fa425002bfd2524be0564447b3a34e7bea6a" :answer/id #uuid "8f156006-40e7-59ee-9535-6dbf94bf76cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3707" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330631/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2aa7a600-0f23-5000-a8c3-fea3674abbed" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330631/field-1/031aaf43793f128e0d888774b282fa425002bfd2524be0564447b3a34e7bea6a" :answer-field/choices ["q-330631/field-1/031aaf43793f128e0d888774b282fa425002bfd2524be0564447b3a34e7bea6a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330631" :question/id #uuid "d0f3f056-0037-536c-89b7-4c45bb247762" :question/math-academy-id "q-330631" :question/problem "| $z$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3783\\,$ | $\\,0.3745\\,$ | $\\,0.3707\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.4168\\,$ | $\\,0.4129\\,$ | $\\,0.4090\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.4562\\,$ | $\\,0.4522\\,$ | $\\,0.4483\\,$ |\n\nThe data above is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z>0.33).$ Use the table above and do not round your answer.\n\n$P(Z>0.33)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/597125714057269b7adf9c0a2a9bbdde9631cf37bc80518281ab4444c3189717.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z∼N(0,1),$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>a)=P(Z<-a)=Φ(-a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z>0.33).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/98cc48cff914158a4c8facf34de162a237e07ba271067aa51ba719a66f17d8af.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z<-0.33).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/357a942bf0b8976c29eedb7f865c381a46c3f841eadfc2203ca3192cea8275af.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(Z>0.33)=P(Z<-0.33)=Φ(-0.33)=0.3707.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-330631/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27018e18-9368-5171-ae78-097adc8bcddf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330631"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330640/field-1/132c0f32c6a14a60c5512c2f8b01d5e79cdd267a726987fbf16f2d47c7627f12" :answer/id #uuid "1681fcdc-34af-5f83-842b-6c1db57ec76c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8051" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330640/field-1/5d4cf146b3144b47e75b465b373090ff86273a4c803e2201512f5cc421e529cc" :answer/id #uuid "ee8e834d-3b70-5a60-a058-f598c6578793" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1949" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330640/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "66e2a9b0-7554-5c27-b8cc-82378ac5b844" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330640/field-1/132c0f32c6a14a60c5512c2f8b01d5e79cdd267a726987fbf16f2d47c7627f12" :answer-field/choices ["q-330640/field-1/132c0f32c6a14a60c5512c2f8b01d5e79cdd267a726987fbf16f2d47c7627f12" "q-330640/field-1/5d4cf146b3144b47e75b465b373090ff86273a4c803e2201512f5cc421e529cc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330640" :question/id #uuid "0d2eba73-714a-5cd1-bbc2-09134cc8459f" :question/math-academy-id "q-330640" :question/problem "| $z$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7704\\,$ | $\\,0.7734\\,$ | $\\,0.7764\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7995\\,$ | $\\,0.8023\\,$ | $\\,0.8051\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8264\\,$ | $\\,0.8289\\,$ | $\\,0.8315\\,$ |\n\nThe data above is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function  $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z>-0.86).$ Use the table above and do not round your answer.\n\n$P(Z>-0.86)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/dc28d78d3f9334aad287ba8e3532b95e4287b84b395d58301016bb056dff2006.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z∼N(0,1)$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>-a)=P(Z<a)=Φ(a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z>-0.86).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/07d788a65e5a5c177e7d1e54a3212c71eb0b36f22ec9f582ebb3ad37c6de8cb7.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z<0.86).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/abdde6b554257a3ed44d091a9a87095af7bde7534b0695f5ac97d6bf24bcb160.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(Z>-0.86)=P(Z<0.86)=Φ(0.86)=0.8051.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-330640/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27018e18-9368-5171-ae78-097adc8bcddf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330640"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330642/field-1/a5f0f3f7c853ba3e3d4af67be3ca9d35c71fcd919b6a5bae34b0b1be658df040" :answer/id #uuid "0e04c705-2510-542d-8f20-a51d2e8f20b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7704" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330642/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f6d165ee-287d-5077-8162-3b1bbf1cadf0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330642/field-1/a5f0f3f7c853ba3e3d4af67be3ca9d35c71fcd919b6a5bae34b0b1be658df040" :answer-field/choices ["q-330642/field-1/a5f0f3f7c853ba3e3d4af67be3ca9d35c71fcd919b6a5bae34b0b1be658df040"] :db/ens