 |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.8023\\,$ | $\\,0.8051\\,$ | $\\,0.8078\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8289\\,$ | $\\,0.8315\\,$ | $\\,0.8340\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.8531\\,$ | $\\,0.8554\\,$ | $\\,0.8577\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/37674375730f32a70d7909a7ab01f3f9c836cf9c72d16447d499af20427f022c.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z∼N(0,1)$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>-a)=P(Z<a)=Φ(a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z>-0.97).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/a8b07524ca3a1ac1750f86e9a5088a07150d7d1b038158e74d924b8811a405a0.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z<0.97).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/ef497f11f5ec451215e923157b6675d16c175dc23ec7d6576bf0a018e3ef594c.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(Z>-0.97)=P(Z<0.97)=Φ(0.97)=0.8340.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-183745/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27018e18-9368-5171-ae78-097adc8bcddf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-183745"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330661/field-1/ae0b7843639408cae439ab36c543a1cd01971987d13477976bd5b6b5c1a331c6" :answer/id #uuid "fd4d7fb5-a796-58ff-828c-e8476b666444" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3520" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330661/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7d20c04-327b-52a3-be58-2634dcf36eaf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330661/field-1/ae0b7843639408cae439ab36c543a1cd01971987d13477976bd5b6b5c1a331c6" :answer-field/choices ["q-330661/field-1/ae0b7843639408cae439ab36c543a1cd01971987d13477976bd5b6b5c1a331c6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330661" :question/id #uuid "c3481bdc-6bb2-5583-85be-5c9f6c24be0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-330661" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z<-0.38).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.6064\\,$ | $\\,0.6103\\,$ | $\\,0.6141\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6443\\,$ | $\\,0.6480\\,$ | $\\,0.6517\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6808\\,$ | $\\,0.6844\\,$ | $\\,0.6879\\,$ |\n\n$P(Z<-0.38)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/8a6467813ccf982906fb5d1d8cd5c5c88b984c22a1e238715c65315a7772249c.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z∼N(0,1),$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>a)=P(Z<-a)=Φ(-a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z<-0.38).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/ee2aebec9953a09dca6eab5c7e5434240885a383a6701638fffdaa9ee9cfeb40.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z>0.38).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/619fae52bde8b2da729095f733e1ea1411132fffe70cc23e252a83cbb2e7ff23.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z<-0.38) & =P(Z>0.38) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<0.38) \\\\  & =1-Φ(0.38) \\\\  & =1-0.6480 \\\\  & =0.3520.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-330661/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a6ee4c7-a51f-5dce-b5c9-2e00acf6bf3e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330661"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/