813ecf007" :question/math-academy-id "q-131532" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z<-0.73).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7673\\,$ | $\\,0.7704\\,$ | $\\,0.7734\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7967\\,$ | $\\,0.7995\\,$ | $\\,0.8023\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8238\\,$ | $\\,0.8264\\,$ | $\\,0.8289\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/597125714057269b7adf9c0a2a9bbdde9631cf37bc80518281ab4444c3189717.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z∼N(0,1),$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>a)=P(Z<-a)=Φ(-a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z<-0.73).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/3e4fb2143266d45a620bf39a978ba8ac4f0ed2585942f79dc90435a4896f9a0d.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z>0.73).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/6bb24449a20276b9d190e2b31926bb6e0d52f22536431e27c05db00b92886ffc.png)\n\nNote that the two shaded areas above have the same area. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z<-0.73) & =P(Z>0.73) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<0.73) \\\\  & =1-Φ(0.73) \\\\  & =1-0.7673 \\\\  & =0.2327.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131532/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a6ee4c7-a51f-5dce-b5c9-2e00acf6bf3e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131532"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-183811/selection/c657f549c0528bd64d18c72d2681949c3cca34b61ce37ee512977a8f34a73978" :answer/i