nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z>-1.63).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/de76fcee7abfd8b2374c2ddc5f038114181ac60fcdbed08ad335f15d196c79a0.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z<1.63) & =P(Z>-1.63) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<-1.63) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-1.63) \\\\  & =1-0.0516 \\\\  & =0.9484.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-330650/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a6ee4c7-a51f-5dce-b5c9-2e00acf6bf3e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330650"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330651/field-1/38dad3160f921cecd315734419af7f030f9beeadaaa7520a89843745da2276e2" :answer/id #uuid "4bec2373-43a9-5043-8a6d-a21b65b12d70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9738" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330651/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5ed6df51-3285-5f85-85d2-b8d4da50e504" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330651/field-1/38dad3160f921cecd315734419af7f030f9beeadaaa7520a89843745da2276e2" :answer-field/choices ["q-330651/field-1/38dad3160f921cecd315734419af7f030f9beeadaaa7520a89843745da2276e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330651" :question/id #uuid "53e3344a-2bac-51b5-a516-8529f57987f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-330651" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z<1.94).$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-2.0\\,$ | $\\,0.0224\\,$ | $\\,0.0217\\,$ | $\\,0.0212\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.9\\,$ | $\\,0.0274\\,$ | $\\,0.0268\\,$ | $\\,0.0262\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.8\\,$ | $\\,0.0344\\,$ | $\\,0.0336\\,$ | $\\,0.0329\\,$ |\n\n$P(Z<1.94)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/0316b85ed769fd2688538ed2c9a47236db0890bf52bf7fcbad021f7d509373b4.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z∼N(0,1)$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>-a)=P(Z<a)=Φ(a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z<1.94).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/e708b9dc6927a17f193c216f1b14b1b9ef98e6d9d26a998790112863661ca5d0.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z>-1.94).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/43f1e2eb5354cbdcd5ff359985048fa2d6411167ad5f50fe45c730642e184b61.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z<1.94) & =P(Z>-1.94) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<-1.94) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-1.94) \\\\  & =1-0.0262 \\\\  & =0.9738.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-330651/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a6ee4c7-a51f-5dce-b5c9-2e00acf6bf3e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330651"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-183828/selection/7c3e6089d17fe19128343292c399b649942e07ef4432343e8347d6f001155664" :answer/id #uuid "a245f0d2-05e2-5b90-b9bf-b9d3808a81ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2167" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183828/selection/e6b5127d5740a71888c20ccbcb0ed4d4dab32f2bbfd0bcb2403412bded7af015" :answer/id #uuid "5d077201-d6f6-5a0c-aedf-e379c25c4206" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2231" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183828/selection/39bc6d168e248f3b2d1175ba47165475c626704f15aff47f8f9a67f3104b5025" :answer/id #uuid "9150e487-f36f-5dd4-9761-ee2d7044a881" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2205" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183828/selection/585124dbfb4d6be1ff5f9db9f7b90d8cd067f8be2ddfb1cdde306fb59975466e" :answer/id #uuid "78c08721-b5fb-5376-bdff-779f7ca32059" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2233" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183828/selection/00d5cacd18ba32068071f98cb1c457f4de1b7c4c75c2574c627dee8bc4b1c1a8" :answer/id #uuid "874f1411-1489-5381-ad31-2981f2f207af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2118" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183828/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea06906b-8fd5-510b-a37e-59e231c5d765" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-183828/selection/585124dbfb4d6be1ff5f9db9f7b90d8cd067f8be2ddfb1cdde306fb59975466e" :answer-field/choices ["q-183828/selection/7c3e6089d17fe19128343292c399b649942e07ef4432343e8347d6f001155664" "q-183828/selection/e6b5127d5740a71888c20ccbcb0ed4d4dab32f2bbfd0bcb2403412bded7af015" "q-183828/selection/39bc6d168e248f3b2d1175ba47165475c626704f15aff47f8f9a67f3104b5025" "q-183828/selection/585124dbfb4d6be1ff5f9db9f7b90d8cd067f8be2ddfb1cdde306fb59975466e" "q-183828/selection/00d5cacd18ba32068071f98cb1c457f4de1b7c4c75c2574c627dee8bc4b1c1a8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-183828" :question/id #uuid "5580ddf0-d280-55cd-87b0-06ddfbc57e68" :question/math-academy-id "q-183828" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(-0.19<Z<0.38).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3557\\,$ | $\\,0.3520\\,$ | $\\,0.3483\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.3936\\,$ | $\\,0.3897\\,$ | $\\,0.3859\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.4325\\,$ | $\\,0.4286\\,$ | $\\,0.4247\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-0.19<Z<0.38).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/bd478e9925303e3d018e2d070e4e3a78e72fb699a48ac3109ddf743158bb5599.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.19<Z<0.38) & =P(Z<0.38)-P(Z\\le -0.19) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.38)-P(Z\\le -0.19) \\\\  & =Φ(0.38)-Φ(-0.19)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-0.38) & =0.3520 \\\\ Φ(-0.19) & =0.4247,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut we are not given $Φ(0.38).$ However, we can compute this using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.38) & =P(Z\\le 0.38) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge -0.38) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<-0.38) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le -0.38) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-0.38) \\\\  & =1-0.3520 \\\\  & =0.6480\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.19<Z<0.38) & =Φ(0.38)-Φ(-0.19) \\\\  & =0.6480-0.4247 \\\\  & =0.2233.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-183828/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "02d2757f-1179-5ad6-b8c7-5165ac3a3eff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-183828"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330889/field-1/5ea21b1caea0f4debec1af132a0d226c1632d30ef7f644b689c2173977aa8c96" :answer/id #uuid "736bb855-85f4-5f7b-bc75-ee71606f7691" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4714" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330889/field-1/426ac6edff681ecd7b50846bf0ddf0fa6010ed3e69184ace73bd581abb690264" :answer/id #uuid "8ee43f02-a302-595a-b20e-7372e1a8c914" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7357" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330889/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "714a5d94-1904-53e6-9913-a93da697a8da" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330889/field-1/5ea21b1caea0f