 the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.18<Z<0.18) & =P(Z<0.18)-P(Z\\le -0.18) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.18)-P(Z\\le -0.18) \\\\  & =Φ(0.18)-Φ(-0.18)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\nΦ(-0.18)=0.4286,\n$$\n\nbut we are not given $Φ(0.18).$ However, we can compute this using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.18) & =P(Z\\le 0.18) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge -0.18) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<-0.18) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le -0.18) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-0.18) \\\\  & =1-0.4286 \\\\  & =0.5714\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.18<Z<0.18) & =Φ(0.18)-Φ(-0.18) \\\\  & =0.5714-0.4286 \\\\  & =0.1428.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-183823/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "02d2757f-1179-5ad6-b8c7-5165ac3a3eff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-183823"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330903/field-1/766ad759fe60d554dc143f01e57d23f6378ffd44f4c548bbff08e8d457c7c5f3" :answer/id #uuid "f2a09873-72ae-5563-a018-35a6603b5255" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8788" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330903/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "351940d9-74b5-510b-a5c5-d01f13c46569" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330903/field-1/766ad759fe60d554dc143f01e57d23f6378ffd44f4c548bbff08e8d457c7c5f3" :answer-field/choices ["q-330903/field-1/766ad759fe60d554dc143f01e57d23f6378ffd44f4c548bbff08e8d457c7c5f3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330903" :question/id #uuid "c14c23d5-7455-50af-9191-550faf7f7f76" :question/math-academy-id "q-330903" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(-1.55<Z<1.55).$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.4\\,$ | $\\,0.9236\\,$ | $\\,0.9251\\,$ | $\\,0.9265\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.5\\,$ | $\\,0.9370\\,$ | $\\,0.9382\\,$ | $\\,0.9394\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.9484\\,$ | $\\,0.9495\\,$ | $\\,0.9505\\,$ |\n\n$P(-1.55<Z<1.55)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-1.55<Z<1.55).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/45d71abed85d91a5a1b150fb741bcc8fa9967f7b2b8d77df35423a909b1e8522.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.55<Z<1.55) & =P(Z<1.55)-P(Z\\le -1.55) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 1.55)-P(Z\\le -1.55) \\\\  & =Φ(1.55)-Φ(-1.55)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\nΦ(1.55)=0.9394,\n$$\n\nbut we are not given $Φ(-1.55).$ However, we can compute this using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.55) & =P(Z\\le -1.55) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge 1.55) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<1.55) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le 1.55) \\\\  & =1-Φ(1.55) \\\\  & =1-0.9394 \\\\  & =0.0606\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.55<Z<1.55) & =Φ(1.55)-Φ(-1.55) \\\\  & =0.9394-0.0606 \\\\  & =0.8788.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-330903/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "02d2757f-1179-5ad6-b8c7-5165ac3a3eff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330903"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-13270"] :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z \\sim N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z \\gt -0.76).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.05 \\,$ | $\\, 0.06 \\,$ | $\\, 0.07 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, 0.6 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7422 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7454 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7486 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.7 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7734 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7764 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7794 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.8 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8023 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8051 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8078 \\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/f88bf9a66694858e9eaf16f616555eda6d9da7de9f62b678bc1f03b32bf9a620.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z \\sim N(0,1)$ we have the following symmetry property for $a > 0{:}$\n\n$$\nP(Z \\gt -a) = P(Z \\lt a) = \\Phi(a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z\\sim N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P( Z > -0.76).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/fbacbbe3f53c73316fd070d95e4c077cd695bdcf884d30a95f6b0850df328c80.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z \\lt 0.76).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/c0f612336c02eee97d6c66b56f0854286b3a23b90053810e9e4fb75b698b5a60.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(Z > -0.76)\n= P(Z < 0.76)\n= \\Phi(0.76)\n= 0.7764.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-13271"] :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z \\sim N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z \\lt -1.54).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.02 \\,$ | $\\, 0.03 \\,$ | $\\, 0.04 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, 1.3 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9066 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9082 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9099 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 1.4 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9222 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9236 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9251 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 1.5 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9357 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9370 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9382 \\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/4d6524ff1e32b2c2b4aaf7481dbf63a96f847cd91ce66aeeb58690f37bbe50e5.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z \\sim N(0,1),$ we have the following symmetry property for $a > 0{:}$\n\n$$\nP(Z \\gt a) = P(Z \\lt -a) = \\Phi(-a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z\\sim N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P( Z \\lt -1.54).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/52d4c1add91819ff1f9dddf609b5753506c26e6cd6ee7f3cb14150ccb9b60971.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z \\gt 1.54).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/7fef056bb5564986a009198685a2951de87ccb8e09c932c6902bfafdcdf0656f.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z<-1.54) & =P(Z>1.54) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<1.54) \\\\  & =1-Φ(1.54) \\\\  & =1-0.9382 \\\\  & =0.0618.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-13269"] :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z \\sim N(0,1),$ compute $P(-0.53 <   Z <        0.53).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.02 \\,$ | $\\, 0.03 \\,$ | $\\, 0.04 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, 0.4 \\,$ | $\\, 0.6628 \\,$ | $\\, 0.6664 \\,$ | $\\, 0.67 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.5 \\,$ | $\\, 0.6985 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7019 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7054 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.6 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7324 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7357 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7389 \\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z\\sim N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-0.53 <        Z <        0.53).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/bb86bde3595d6a64d1cd82da3c928f28c496f495f9c6815e56ee025a4a69d685.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z \\leq z) = \\Phi(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $\\Phi(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.53<Z<0.53) & =P(Z<0.53)-P(Z\\le -0.53) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.53)-P(Z\\le -0.53) \\\\  & =Φ(0.53)-Φ(-0.53)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\n\\Phi(0.53) = 0.7019,\n$$\n\nbut we are not given $\\Phi(-0.53) .$ However, we can compute this using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-0.53) & =P(Z\\le -0.53) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge 0.53) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<0.53) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le 0.53) \\\\  & =1-Φ(0.53) \\\\  & =1-0.7019 \\\\  & =0.2981\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.53<Z<0.53) & =Φ(0.53)-Φ(-0.53) \\\\  & =0.7019-0.2981 \\\\  & =0.4038.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
